  "scope": "The pinned full exact game proves unrestricted PXC91c false at n=6 under both the strong fixed-Cx and weaker existential-Cx readings. This artifact alone does not establish the global minimum failure dimension; the separate PXC100 exact-cone theorem exhausts n=5 and supplies that lower bound. The auxiliary search is exact for every listed game and every qualifying cover; all complete Cx row subsets only when the x-tight pool is within the stated threshold. The generator bank is exhaustive only for disjoint-support two-generator integer lower envelopes through the stated total; the n6 archives are finite. Archive exactness/selectors are source-pinned rather than independently replayed unless a witness is promoted, in which case missing replay is explicit. The auxiliary null results are discovery controls rather than the n=5 proof; that proof is the 3,840-cell unrestricted_pxc91c_n5_all_cells.py census together with its raw PXC92b and independent normalized-incidence cell encodings."
